# NPSSO is a BOOTSTRAP SEED, read only while KV holds no token — it carries a
# first deploy, and the first paste through /admin retires it. Renew a live
# token there, never here: this one cannot be written at runtime.
# The KV pair is pulled into .env.local by `vercel env pull`. For local work,
# .env.dev.local loads last and blanks it so dev cannot reach the production
# store. See that file for the dev-redis recipe.
NPSSO=
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=

# Steam. The key is per-account from steamcommunity.com/dev/apikey; the id is
# the 64-bit one, not the vanity name — the vanity does not resolve.
# The steam-game verb additionally needs "Game details" set to Public in Steam's
# privacy settings, which is separate from "My profile".
STEAM_API_KEY=
STEAM_ID64=

# The admin area at /admin — hide games, paste a fresh NPSSO. All three must be
# set or every admin route answers 503; there is no open fallback.
# ADMIN_SECRET signs the session cookie: `openssl rand -hex 32`.
ADMIN_EMAIL=
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
ADMIN_SECRET=
